# Code Ansys — README (brief)

Purpose
- Scripts / project files to run ANSYS simulations used by the thesis.

Key files
- [Code Ansys/CodeProject](Code Ansys/CodeProject) — ANSYS project / input script.
- [Code Ansys/CodeProject_Video](Code Ansys/CodeProject_Video) — backup / video version.
- [Code Ansys/Input_PositionPatches.txt](Code Ansys/Input_PositionPatches.txt) — patch center positions used by ANSYS.
- [Code Ansys/Input_GeometricParameters.txt](Code Ansys/Input_GeometricParameters.txt) — geometric parameters written by MATLAB driver.
- [Code Ansys/Input_EletricValues.txt](Code Ansys/Input_EletricValues.txt) — electrical excitation parameters.
- [Code Ansys/Output_DataAmplitude.txt](Code Ansys/Output_DataAmplitude.txt) — amplitude output (used for analysis).
- [Code Ansys/Output_DataFrequency.txt](Code Ansys/Output_DataFrequency.txt) — frequency output.
- [Code Ansys/Output_EMCC.txt](Code Ansys/Output_EMCC.txt) — EMCC outputs read by MATLAB.

How it is used (quick)
- MATLAB writes Input_*.txt files and calls the ANSYS batch executable (see DMS folder `funcFF.m`).
- After ANSYS finishes, MATLAB reads Output_*.txt files and uses them to compute objective values.

Notes
- Keep ANSYS path and permission to run the ANSYS executable.